    "interpretation": "1. 6-Class Task (Chance = 16.67%): The metadata (52.00%) and strict nuisance (52.67%) probes achieve ~52% primarily because SILENCE is separated with 100% precision (75/75) due to lack of speech energy, and speech vs silence envelope separation provides an initial coarse split.\n2. 4-Target Task (Chance = 25.00%): When trained and evaluated strictly on the four target keywords (TRAI, PHAI, LEN, XUONG), the strict nuisance probe achieves 55.00% overall accuracy with class-dependent performance (LEN: 69/75, PHAI: 39/75, TRAI: 34/75, XUONG: 23/75), indicating potential residual nuisance associations without establishing causality. Descriptive subset accuracy on the 150 TRAI and PHAI ground-truth samples is 48.67% (73/150), with a conditional ratio of true TRAI among predicted TRAI on that subset of 50.75% (34/67) and full-task TRAI precision of 37.78% (34/90). The metadata probe (52.67%) outputs identical aggregate prediction counts ([30, 45, 0, 0]) for true TRAI and true PHAI.\n3. Binary Task (Majority = 66.67%): Nuisance features achieve 80.89% binary detection of speech presence versus silence/short foils.\n4. Conclusion: TC-ResNet-14 achieves 100.00% accuracy across the 4 targets on the synthetic test set, demonstrating that learned representations support strong class separation on the tested synthetic distributions. This empirical finding does not prove genuine Vietnamese phonetic recognition or that formant trajectories are the proven causal basis, as controlled causal phonetic interventions were not conducted."
